PreTrained Deep Learning Models | Computer Vision

Published: 27 July 2018

The article discusses popular pre-trained models for Computer Vision and how they can be used for Transfer Learning instead of training a neural network from scratch.

Main Models Covered
--------------------

| Model                 | Year | Main Use                 | Real-Time Example                 |
| --------------------- | ---- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------- |
| LeNet-5               | 1998 | Digit Recognition        | Bank cheque reading               |
| AlexNet               | 2012 | Image Classification     | Identifying objects in photos     |
| VGG16                 | 2014 | Feature Extraction       | Product image search              |
| VGG19                 | 2014 | Image Classification     | Medical image analysis            |
| GoogLeNet (Inception) | 2014 | Efficient Classification | Google Photos                     |
| ResNet                | 2015 | Deep Image Recognition   | Self-driving cars                 |
| InceptionV3           | 2015 | Image Classification     | Image tagging systems             |
| Xception              | 2017 | Advanced Classification  | Defect detection in manufacturing |
| MobileNet             | 2017 | Mobile Vision            | Smartphone camera AI              |
| DenseNet              | 2017 | Feature Reuse            | Medical diagnostics               |


=========

Why These Models Are Important

Before these models:

❌ Developers needed millions of images and days of training.

After these models:

✅ Download pre-trained weights

✅ Apply Transfer Learning

✅ Train with a few hundred or thousand images

✅ Get high accuracy quickly

